./worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/fa_orbit_codex_chunk_kit_review.md:18:DESIGN: (1) fa_orbit_ckpt_preflight.py --chain: same INITIAL-identity binding as --extension but the resume anchor is the TIP of arms.<ARM>.chain (links written only by the recorder); empty chain refuses; optional --chunk-end validated (multiple of 2500, EXPECTED_STEP < N <= budget). (2) fa_orbit_record_restart.py: a manifest carrying chunk_end is recorded as an immutable chain link {job, uuid, manifest sha, resume_step/sha, final_step=chunk_end, final_ckpt_sha256 hashed from the on-disk endpoint ckpt}; idempotent per job; content-drift on re-record refuses; identity checks parameterized (anchor/tip, CHUNK wall pin). (3) fa_orbit_submit.sh --chunk-end: shape checks + CHUNK time pin + exports CHUNK_END. (4) fa_orbit_train.sbatch: STOPSTEP=CHUNK_END feeds train.py --max-steps AND the completion-literal classifier; budget pin unmoved; preflight dispatch: EXPECTED_STEP==40000 -> --extension, >40000 -> --chain; CHUNK pins; manifest chunk_end line. (5) NEW fa_orbit_chunk_watchdog.sh: KV-whitelist args, per-arm: skip if job named exp11-<ARM>-train queued; find newest canonical ckpt step S; S>=TARGET -> done; if S>40000 and registry tip<S record the finished chunk first (unique manifest by chunk_end==S, recorder refusal -> failure); submit next chunk via the sanctioned submitter only; 2 consecutive failures freeze the arm (state file, human-clearable); ONESHOT/DRYRUN test hooks. (6) 22 new guard cases, all passing (113 pass total; 5 pre-existing dirty-tree submitter cases clear on commit).
./worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/fa_orbit_codex_chunk_kit_review.md:20:REVIEW FOCUS: (a) can any sequence of watchdog + recorder + preflight actions launder an unrecorded/foreign checkpoint into the lineage, or double-submit an arm (race between squeue check and submit; job-name collisions with the five OLD long legs still queued as exp11-<ARM>-train — we cancel them before starting the watchdog, is anything else vulnerable)? (b) recorder correctness: link append under concurrent invocation (store lock?), atomic write, the mine/at indexing, chunk_end vs budget/cadence edges; (c) preflight --chain: any bypass via crafted registry/manifest (note the resume file is always re-hashed); (d) launcher: STOPSTEP interactions with the completion literal, argv-parity section G, wandb fresh-id (r4) under many chunks, TIME_PIN selection; (e) watchdog: sacct settle logic (CANCELLED counts as failure — is that right when a human scancels?), leg_manifest_for uniqueness under repeated same-boundary attempts after a failed leg (two manifests with chunk_end==S -> permanent freeze — is the recovery path documented/sound?), state-file semantics; (f) the 2500-step chunk size: startup overhead ~10-15min/leg at 8 GPUs — flag if you consider the overhead-to-compute ratio for any arm unacceptable vs a 5000-step chunk. Verdict: BLOCKING/NON-BLOCKING findings then APPROVED or REVISE.
